# Domain Terminology

Full reference: `docs/domain-glossary.md`

## Name Disambiguation

- `RefPMS` (or `프로젝트` when referring to this software) = the software itself.
- `Project` (hierarchy term) = the domain-level piping/plant project whose global constraints govern all Classes and Components.
- When ambiguous, always clarify: *"RefPMS (the software) or Project (the domain hierarchy)?"*

## Decision Hierarchy

Three layers; upstream Constraints limit downstream choices.

| Layer | Role |
|---|---|
| `Project` | Global premises and constraints (design code, units, NPS master, thread standards) |
| `Class` | Inherits Project constraints + adds classification constraints (Piping Material Classification) |
| `Component` | Inherits Class constraints + specifies shape, characteristics, and detailed specs to produce a unique item |

**NEVER** use `Material` as the name of the lowest hierarchy level. `Material` may be confused with `재질` (metallurgical material), which is only one attribute of a Component.

## Core Concepts — Mandatory Distinctions

| Term | Definition | Key Question |
|---|---|---|
| `Constraint` | Mandatory limit or permissible range — must be respected | *What must be?* |
| `Condition` | Observable state, premise, or input fact evaluated for a Decision | *What is?* |
| `Rule` | Decision logic that takes Conditions + Constraints and determines an outcome; designed from Domain Knowledge | *What should be decided?* |
| `Validation` | Conformance check — verifies whether input/setting meets established criteria | *Is it valid?* |
| `Default` | Standard selection applied when the user has not explicitly specified a value; always overridable, never overrides a Constraint | *What applies if unspecified?* |
| `Domain Knowledge` | Professional expertise that determines exceptions, priorities, and special judgments; the source from which Rules are designed | *Why this rule?* |

## Precedence

```
Constraint  >  Rule  >  Default
```

An Override at a lower scope must still satisfy all applicable Constraints.

## Prohibited Confusions

- Do NOT use "조건" alone — always specify `Condition` or `Constraint`.
- Do NOT conflate `Rule` and `Validation` — Rule decides; Validation checks.
- Do NOT treat `Default` as mandatory — Defaults are overridable; Constraints are not.
- Do NOT call the lowest hierarchy level `Material` — use `Component`.
- Do NOT reduce `Class` to a simple data-entry form — Class is a classification layer with its own constraints.

